// The Veteran cape, for the players who tested the server before it opened.
//
// THE MODELS ARE GENERATED, NOT HAND-EDITED. tools/models/genveterancape.py builds all three from
// the Attack cape's: the skillcape shape recoloured to bronze, with Jagex's attack emblem cut out
// of the mesh and the server's DP monogram built in its place. The emblem on this cape is
// geometry rather than a texture - the 377 client has none on this model - so swapping it means
// deleting twenty-four faces and adding eighty-eight. Rerun the generator rather than editing the
// .ob2 files.
//
// The bronze is the same ramp the Veteran chat icon is drawn in, so the rank reads as one thing
// in chat and on the back. The monogram is the brand's red, because a bronze monogram on a bronze
// cape disappears.
//
// NO RECOLOURS HERE, unlike every other cape in the build. The colours are baked into the
// generated models instead. The skillcapes share one mesh and recolour it per skill, which needs
// a list of colour pairs per item - and the inventory mesh and the worn mesh of this cape do not
// share all their source colours, so such a list silently leaves one of the two models the wrong
// colour. Generating the models with the colour already in them cannot go wrong that way.
//
// THE DEFENCE IS A PLAIN CAPE'S, deliberately. This is a badge: a reward that is also an upgrade
// would pull against the launch wipe, which exists to put everyone on the same footing. A Cape of
// Accomplishment's +9 would have made it worth wearing for its stats.
//
// Untradeable, and given back by the server to any veteran who does not have one - see
// Engine-TS World.grantVeteranCape. Losing it costs nothing but a relog.

[veteran_cape]
name=Veteran cape
desc=Worn by those who tested Death Plateau before it opened.
model=obj_veteran_cape
manwear=obj_veteran_cape_manwear,0
womanwear=obj_veteran_cape_womanwear,0
// The Attack cape's own 2d camera, since this is its mesh.
2dzoom=2128
2dxan=504
2dyof=1
iop2=Wear
wearpos=back
cost=1
tradeable=no
weight=1lb
category=armour_cape
param=slashdefence,1
param=crushdefence,1
param=rangedefence,2
